**What this means for you:** Natural asscher studs make practical sense in one specific scenario — you require natural-origin diamonds for the pair. In that case, yellow gold is the better metal than white gold; the warm metal partially absorbs the H-I stone's color warmth, reducing the Forward-Face Effect's visibility impact. Platinum adds $100-350 per size over white gold and eliminates rhodium replating — for earrings worn daily over decades, the maintenance advantage is genuine. At the 1/4ct tw entry ($900 natural YG vs $438 lab WG), the gap is $462 for objectively lower quality — only choose natural if origin matters to you.

