## Understanding Total Carat Weight in Asscher Stud Earrings

All asscher stud earrings are sold in matched pairs with total carat weight — the combined weight of both stones.

A 1ct tw pair has two stones, each approximately 0.50ct. A 1/2ct tw pair has two stones, each approximately 0.25ct. The "per ear" column in all tables above reflects this — it is the individual stone size per earring.

**Size guide by visual impact at ear distance:**

At 1/4ct tw (0.12ct per ear), the asscher step-cut reads as a small, precise geometric presence. The Hall of Mirrors is there — compact and defined. Good for subtle everyday wear where the asscher's shape is the interest, not the size.

At 1/2ct tw (0.25ct per ear), the asscher begins to show its geometry clearly at conversational distance. The step-cut facets are visible. This is the minimum size where the Forward-Face Effect fully activates — the octagonal Hall of Mirrors reads at 6-12 inches.

At 3/4ct tw (0.38ct per ear), the asscher stud sits as a confident geometric statement. The step-cut depth is clearly visible; the Hall of Mirrors shows its stacked reflections at face level. Good balance between everyday wearability and visible presence.

At 1ct tw (0.50ct per ear), the asscher stud is a clear architectural window at face level. The Hall of Mirrors reads immediately and boldly. This is the statement size for daily wear — noticeable without being oversized.

At 2ct tw (1ct per ear), the asscher stud is an unmistakably bold choice. Each stone is a full 1ct step-cut geometric window facing the viewer. Reserved for buyers who want the earrings to be the focal point — and who want a pair that almost nobody else in the room will be wearing.

Farzana's guidance: "The 1/2ct tw lab pair is where I usually start buyers who want the asscher look without it dominating. Below that, you have the shape but it's quiet — at 1ct tw, the step-cut is what people notice first. Decide which experience you want before you choose the size."

