## Expert Summary

Asscher cut diamond stud earrings are among the most unusual diamond studs available. Most buyers default to round brilliant. The asscher stud is rare — and its specific optical behavior makes the buying decision more consequential than it first appears.

The Mirror Pair Problem and the Forward-Face Effect are the two principles that define how to buy asscher studs. Two step-cut windows at face level, both facing the viewer simultaneously — this is the format where quality is most directly visible. H-I/SI1-SI2 natural pairs carry both color and clarity risk in precisely the position and format where those attributes are most exposed.

Lab pairs solve both problems — F-G color faces up white in any metal, and VS2 clarity keeps both Hall of Mirrors windows clean. Lab pairs ship matched from the same quality lot. The price is $828 for a 1ct tw pair that grades better than natural asscher studs at any price in this catalog.

> **Farzana's take:** I love the asscher stud for one specific reason. It is a diamond that faces you honestly — two of them, side by side, at face level, every time you talk to someone. It does not hide behind sparkle. That is why quality matters more here than people expect. And it is why lab is the clear answer for asscher studs. You are wearing two step-cut windows that will show what they are made of every day. Get the cleanest matched pair you can. At $828 for a lab 1ct tw pair in F-G/VS2-SI1, there is genuinely no reason not to.

